From 741c5d4a566bdbb1ec7e8f70b1d35e5cd8d8744e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yichao Yu <yyc1992@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:48:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 13/21] newuoa: use BLAS for the model products for n >= 100

With an external BLAS/LAPACK and n >= 100, compute the Hessian-vector
product of the trust-region subproblem (TRSAPP; HD = XPT^T (PQ .* (XPT D)),
with NPT more doubles of workspace), the VLAG/BETA products of each
iteration and the XBASE shift's BMAT updates with DGEMV, DDOT, DAXPY and
DGER.  For smaller n, and without an external BLAS, the original loops
are used: below n = 100, single-threaded OpenBLAS DGEMV made some sizes
up to 3x slower than the loops (depending on the placement of the
arrays), while above it the BLAS version was never slower.

The summation order changes with BLAS, so results differ in the last
bits for n >= 100.  With a cheap objective, the time per evaluation
drops by 1.5x (n = 150) to 1.7x (n = 100, 200).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 CMakeLists.txt           |   4 +-
 src/algs/newuoa/newuoa.c | 106 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 src/util/nlopt-blas.h    |   1 +
 3 files changed, 104 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 014bbd3..dcdb4d1 100644
